Package: raye-scx
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: sched_ext CPU schedulers used while a game runs
 Two CPU schedulers written in BPF that the kernel loads at run time
 and drops by itself if they stop answering:
  - scx_lavd, which keeps frame times steady in games (the 1 % lows)
    when the game competes with downloads, a browser or shader
    compilation;
  - scx_bpfland, tuned for a responsive desktop under load.
 Nothing starts them on its own: Raye's Game mode turns one on while a
 game runs and off when it ends.
